sections.text:
Hypertrophy with valvular insufficiency;
pulse small and weak; unable to rest in a reclining
position. Palpitation during coitus. Failing compensa-
tion, dyspnoea worse lying on left side. Weight and
oppression of heart; as if a hand were squeezing it;
tickling sensation about heart.

Compare: Sccale; Convallar.; Bry.;
Puls.; Rhodod. Gnipsine — active principle — (exalts
the hypotensive properties of Viscum).
